{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. You’re here because of chest pain, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. It started about a week ago. I went to the ER two days ago, but they sent me home and the pain hasn’t gone away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. They mentioned your troponin was elevated, but no EKG changes or echo issues. Can you describe the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s in the center of my chest, like a heavy pressure. It comes and goes, lasts 20 minutes to an hour. Nothing helps except strong pain meds like morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And does it get worse with activity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, walking makes it worse. Yesterday it even spread to my left shoulder and jaw. I also felt tingling in my left arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Those are concerning symptoms. We’ll monitor you closely. We’ve already done a chest X-ray, and it shows no pneumonia or fluid in the lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it my heart again? I had a stent placed a while back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly what we’re checking. Given your history, we’re treating this seriously. We’ve started cardiac monitoring and will repeat blood tests, including troponin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also feel kind of unsteady on my feet. Is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2145-11-05 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be from several things—maybe your blood pressure, medications, or even your VP shunt. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2145-11-05 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your repeat troponin back. It’s still elevated, but stable. No new changes on EKG. We’re admitting you for observation and further testing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2145-11-05 22:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a heart attack then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2145-11-05 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can’t rule it out completely. The elevation suggests heart strain. We’ll do more tests tomorrow, possibly a stress test or angiogram if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2145-11-05 22:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared. I’ve had so many health issues already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2145-11-05 22:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You’ve been through a lot. We’re here to make sure nothing serious is missed. We’ll take it step by step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the chest pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, same pressure. I haven’t walked much because I’m afraid it’ll come on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to do a CT angiogram this morning to check your coronary arteries. It’s a scan that uses contrast to look for blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, just a small IV. You’ll lie still for about 20 minutes. We need to make sure your kidneys are okay first since the dye can affect them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My kidneys have been off before. I had acute kidney failure last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2145-11-06 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. We’ve checked your creatinine, and it’s slightly elevated. We’ll use less contrast and hydrate you well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT angiogram is back. Good news—no major blockages in your coronary arteries. Your stent is open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s unlikely to be a new blockage. The troponin rise could be from strain due to high blood pressure or heart failure. We’re calling it ‘demand ischemia’—your heart needed more oxygen than it got."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the pain radiating and the tingling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Those can still happen with cardiac strain, even without a blockage. But we’re also considering other causes like GERD, which you’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had diarrhea and belly pain too. Could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2145-11-06 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Some heart pain can feel like indigestion. But we’ll treat your GI symptoms separately. We’ll hold off on NSAIDs since you’re allergic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2145-11-06 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs also show mild anemia. It’s not severe, but it could make you feel more tired or short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2145-11-06 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should we find out why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2145-11-06 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can check further as an outpatient. For now, we’ll focus on stabilizing your heart and symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2145-11-06 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also watching your leg swelling. It’s likely from heart failure, which you have a history of."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2145-11-06 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be on a diuretic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2145-11-06 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re cautious because of your kidney function. We’ll start a low dose and monitor your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re planning to discharge you today. Your pain has improved, and no new issues came up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If chest pain returns, especially with jaw or arm pain, call 911. Also monitor for worsening shortness of breath or swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Cardiology in one week. We’ll also schedule GI for your abdominal pain and GERD. Keep using your CPAP for sleep apnea—it helps your heart too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better knowing we checked everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2145-11-07 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send all the info to your primary doctor. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2145-11-07 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—your discharge papers are ready. You’ll get prescriptions for your diuretic, heart meds, and acid reducer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2145-11-07 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll pick them up before I leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2145-11-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—we noticed a small spot on your lung from an old scan. It’s likely benign, but we’ll follow up with a repeat CT in a few months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2145-11-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it cancer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2145-11-07 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No evidence of that. It’s called a solitary pulmonary nodule—very common and usually harmless. We just monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2145-11-07 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will come by with your discharge instructions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2145-11-07 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2145-11-07 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Stay safe and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2145-11-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check—how are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2145-11-07 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Chest pain is gone, and I feel steady on my feet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2145-11-07 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. You’re cleared to go home. Take it easy for the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2145-11-07 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2145-11-07 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Get some rest and follow up as scheduled."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
